{"v":1,"accession":"PRJDB4212","title":"Dynamics of a simulated riparian micobiome treating severely polluted urban effluent","description":"Changes in microbial communities analysed using high throughput sequencing and correlations with physico-chemical properties of a rhizofiltration system treating severely polluted urban effluent.  The aim of the study was to describe the dynamics of microbes associated with the rhizomes of wetland plants growing in an urban effluent phytoremediation system. High throughput sequencing technology was used the characterize the bacterial communities, with the objective of determining their response to high pollutant loads which included nutrients and human associated microflora. Ultimately this work contributed to a better understanding of the potential mechanisms involved in pollutant removal through urban effluent best management practices.","center":"Stellenbosch University","data_type":"Targeted Locus (Loci)","submission_date":"2016/12/30 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMD00040681","Unplanted control 1_0C","probable_urban","soil_greenspace","2014-04-18",2014,"ZA","Western Cape",6951112,"Somerset West","probable",-33.9433,18.8242,"South Africa:Stellenbosch Wastewater Treament Works",null,"Rhizofiltration system/Constructed wetland/Riparian zone","sand filter bed unplanted","Coarse sand","city-level location without sample-site confirmation"],["SAMD00040682","Bulk sand 1_0RB","probable_urban","soil_greenspace","2014-04-18",2014,"ZA","Western Cape",6951112,"Somerset West","probable",-33.9433,18.8242,"South Africa:Stellenbosch Wastewater Treament Works",null,"Rhizofiltration system/Constructed wetland/Riparian zone","sand filter bed planted","Coarse sand","city-level location wit